; CoreIR sample, family: isolation (rt.isolate_enter, rt.isolate_leave, a handler
; opened by rt.isolate_catch, the cause-cell transfer). FORM #101, FAIL-10, FAIL-16.
;
; Source (package samples@0, module isolate):
;   i0  fn check(x: u64) -> u64 { if x == 0 { unwrap_failed() }; x }
;       resource Temp { id: u64 } drop { if self.id % 2 == 0 { bounds_failed() } }
;       fn guarded(x: u64) -> u64 { let t = Temp { id: x }; check(x) }
;       fn iso(x: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64)     ; isolate(|| guarded(x)), the outcome as words
;       fn twice(x: u64) -> u64 { let _ = iso(x); check(x) }
;       fn outer(x: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64)   ; isolate(|| twice(x))
;       resource Guard { id: u64 } grant 72 drop { let _ = iso(0) }
;       fn during(x: u64) -> u64 { let g = Guard { id: 9 }; check(x) }
;
; iso and outer return (0, available, 0) for Error(Capacity), (1, r, 0) for Ok(Ok(r)),
; and (2, count, kinds) for Ok(Error(causes)): the chain's length and its kinds, primary
; first, as base-16 digits (CauseKind order: Unwrap 3, Bounds 1). They drop the Causes
; before returning. The isolate's cell is 32 (MEM-24), admitted from the current limit
; before the body runs; Temp is 40 (storage 8, cell 32), Guard 112 (storage 8, cell 32,
; grant 72). The root's primary cell is outside its limit.
;
; Behaviour, derived by hand (trace: Temp and Guard ids in the order their cleanup started):
; run: f3(3) -> 1, 3, 0 | used 0 | trace 3             ; returned: the cell is refunded
; run: f3(1) -> 1, 1, 0 | used 0 | trace 1
; Caught after the body's cleanup, with the cause that cleanup added (Unwrap in the
; primary cell, Bounds in Temp's). The failure used the task's primary, so the reserved
; cell is the primary now: dropping the Causes refunds Temp's cell, and 32 stays.
; run: f3(0) -> 2, 2, 49 | used 32 | trace 0
; Temp's finalizer fails on the normal exit, so the primary cause is in Temp's cell and
; the task's primary is unused: the reserved cell is refunded, and nothing stays.
; run: f3(2) -> 2, 1, 1 | used 0 | trace 2
; The reservation is refused before the body runs (31 < 32): Error, nothing made.
; run limit 31: f3(3) -> 0, 31, 0 | used 0
; The reservation is held while the body runs: 71 - 32 leaves 39 < 40 for Temp, so
; guarded's refused construction is the caught Unwrap, which used the primary.
; run limit 71: f3(0) -> 2, 1, 3 | used 32
; Nested: the inner isolate's cell becomes the primary at its catch; check then fails
; into that cell, and the outer catch puts its own cell in its place.
; run: f5(0) -> 2, 1, 3 | used 32 | trace 0
; run: f5(2) -> 1, 2, 0 | used 0 | trace 2             ; inner caught Bounds, refunded
; run: f5(3) -> 1, 3, 0 | used 0 | trace 3
; An isolate inside a finalizer: its body's Unwrap goes into Guard's cell, the obligation of
; the finalizer that runs, and the caught chain leaves with the Causes; the reserved cell, admitted
; from the grant, takes Guard's place and is refunded when the finalizer ends.
; run: f7(5) -> 5 | used 0 | trace 9, 0
; The same during failure cleanup: the active chain (check's Unwrap) is set aside at the
; inner entry and restored at its catch, so the failure goes on with exactly its own cause.
; run: f7(0) -> fail Unwrap | used 0 | trace 9, 0
